<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Gaming on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/gaming/</link><description>Recent content in Gaming on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/gaming/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Doomheaven Moves to GitHub Pages</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/doomheaven-github-pages/</link><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/doomheaven-github-pages/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://doomheaven.uk"&gt;doomheaven.uk&lt;/a&gt; is moving house.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It started life as a Doom fan site back in the late 90s — WADs, screenshots, whatever bits of Doom nonsense felt worth putting on the web at the time. It&amp;rsquo;s sat online quietly ever since, hosted the whole way through by &lt;a href="https://teamhellspawn.com"&gt;teamhellspawn.com&lt;/a&gt;, who&amp;rsquo;ve now let me know they&amp;rsquo;re winding things down.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I want to say a proper thank you to them for that. Free webspace for the better part of three decades is a genuinely long time to keep something ticking over for no reason beyond being decent about it, and rather than just switching it off, they gave me the chance to get everything off in one piece before it went. Not everyone bothers with that on the way out, so it was appreciated.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Steam World Dig</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/steamworlddig/</link><pubDate>Thu, 20 Jan 2022 16:18:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/steamworlddig/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Picked this indie retro style platform game for my Playstation 5 cheap recently.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It was released in 